Security: Switch off PHP's session upload progress

The shipped .user.ini (PHP-FPM, CGI) and .htaccess (Apache with mod_php) now
switch off PHP's session upload progress. owncloud.online does not use it, but
while it is on, anyone can make PHP write data of their choice into the session
storage with a form field named PHP_SESSION_UPLOAD_PROGRESS, without logging
in. The .htaccess gets a block for mod_php.c, the module name of PHP 8; its
existing PHP values only cover mod_php5 and mod_php7 and never applied with
PHP 8. That block only carries this setting.
